<title>USA: Fleetwood Enterprises Q2 sales, net rise.</title>
<headline>Fleetwood Enterprises Q2 sales, net rise.</headline>
<dateline>RIVERSIDE, Calif. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.68		    $0.52</p>
<p> Net			 25,772		   24,011</p>
<p> Sales		    748,780		  707,086</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  37,837		   46,496</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr		 $2.15		    $1.01</p>
<p> Net		 89,882		   46,809</p>
<p> Sales	     1,500,025		1,411,803</p>
<p> Avg shrs	  41,877		   46,507</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: 1995 Q2 includes income from discontinued operations of $2,172,000 or $0.05 per share of Fleetwood Credit Corp before its sale in May 1996.  </p>
<p>Included in current half earnings is an after-tax gain of $33,891,000 on the sale of Fleetwood Credit Corp. First half earnings also include $887,000 or $0.02 per share for one month of operations from Fleetwood Credit.</p>
<p>1996 Q2 benefited from fewer outstanding shares resulting from significant share repurchases over the past few months.</p>
</text>
